course: dictionary
lesson: 3525
title: Fay: a fairy or a name?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which meaning is right. Ask yourself: is this sentence about magic and old stories, or about a person? «The fays of the forest danced in the moonlight» is about magic. «Fay waved to her friend at the bus stop» is about a person.
explain: Fay is an old, poetic word for a fairy, a small magical being. Writers use it to make a story feel old-fashioned and enchanting. The same spelling is also a woman's first name, so always check the sentence before you decide.
explain: Sound can help you remember a word, but the meaning always comes from the context. The French «le café» is said "ka-FAY", so its ending rhymes with fay. That tells you how to say it, not what it means.
fact: A fay is an old or poetic word for a fairy, a small magical being.
fact: Morgan le Fay is a magical woman, an enchantress, in the stories of King Arthur.
fact: In King Arthur stories, Morgan le Fay is Arthur's half-sister and a sorceress.
fact: Fay and Faye are also a woman's first name.
fact: Context tells you which meaning of a word is right: look at the words around it.
exercise: «The fays of the forest danced in the moonlight.» What does fay mean here? | A kind of tree | A woman's first name | *A fairy, a small magical being | A shiny coin
exercise: «Fay waved to her friend at the bus stop.» What is Fay in this sentence? | A grey, wet day | A fairy | A king's castle | *A woman's first name
exercise: Which stories is Morgan le Fay from? | Grandad's dreich Scottish tales | *King Arthur stories | Stories about a school trip
test: Morgan le Fay is an enchantress in which stories? | Stories of Robin Hood | *Stories of King Arthur | Stories of the Roman army
test: In old poems, what does fay usually mean? | A school bag | A petrol station | *A fairy | A brown colour
exam: In «Fay and Faye are my cousins», Fay means what? | A type of forest | *A woman's first name | A kind of bird | A magical being in old stories
